From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rossf <2877553+rossf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:22:46 +0800
Subject: fix: allow blocking in-memory DOM storage shutdown

In-memory LevelDB destruction can wait for background compaction. Declare
MayBlock on the DOM storage task runner while retaining its existing sync
and BLOCK_SHUTDOWN traits. No authentication behavior or checks change.

Preserves the separately validated Chromium 150 storage fix. This temporary
patch has not been submitted or landed upstream. Remove it when the pinned
GetTaskRunnerForDb already grants blocking permission for in-memory databases
and the storage_blocking_contract_test passes with DCHECKs enabled.

Assisted-By: OpenAI Codex

diff --git a/components/services/storage/dom_storage/dom_storage_database.cc b/components/services/storage/dom_storage/dom_storage_database.cc
index 09293b730fdbe1df011227653580ac2519001f22..128e66380a4df99ff7c2ca4f01905467d653c721 100644
--- a/components/services/storage/dom_storage/dom_storage_database.cc
+++ b/components/services/storage/dom_storage/dom_storage_database.cc
@@ -267,8 +267,9 @@ scoped_refptr<base::SequencedTaskRunner> GetTaskRunnerForDb(
     const base::FilePath& database_path) {
   if (database_path.empty()) {
-    // For the in-memory case, blocking shutdown is only important to avoid
-    // leaking the SequenceBound on shutdown (and triggering ASAN failures).
+    // An in-memory LevelDB can still wait for background compaction during
+    // destruction. Its condition-variable wait requires blocking permission.
+    // Block shutdown to avoid leaking the SequenceBound (and ASAN failures).
     return base::ThreadPool::CreateSequencedTaskRunner(
-        {base::WithBaseSyncPrimitives(),
+        {base::MayBlock(), base::WithBaseSyncPrimitives(),
          base::TaskShutdownBehavior::BLOCK_SHUTDOWN});
   }
